WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.110
When it premiered on ABC in September of 1993,
NYPD Blue made television history with its

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.760
gritty portrayal of the exploits of Manhattan's
15th police precinct.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.911
Using documentary-style camerawork and a healthy
dose of PG-13 material, creators Steven Bochco

00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:19.840
and David Milch ushered network television
into a bold new era of creative storytelling.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.660
During its 12-season run, the show formed
a solid ensemble of talented actors, many

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.450
of whom got their big break on the critically
acclaimed series.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.300
Let's look back at some of the most notable
NYPD Blue cast members and discover what they've

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.060
been up to since turning in their badges.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.609
David Caruso

00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:39.089
Prior to busting perps as Detective John Kelly,
David Caruso had a solid career, from playing

00:00:39.089 --> 00:00:43.089
a cop in Rambo: First Blood, to playing a
gang leader in Bochco's groundbreaking series

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:44.499
Hill Street Blues.

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:48.889
The success of NYPD Blue launched Caruso onto
the A list — and he famously left the show

00:00:48.889 --> 00:00:52.959
after the first season to star in forgettable
films like Kiss of Death… which pretty much

00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:56.269
described Caruso's attempts at big-screen
stardom.

00:00:56.269 --> 00:01:01.100
Caruso revitalized his career by returning
to TV for 10 seasons of CSI: Miami.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.239
As Lieutenant Horatio Caine, his penchant
for puns and dark sunglasses achieved pretty

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.239
epic meme status.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.960
"Friend said she came down to drink mojitos
and catch some sun."

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.660
"Well it looks like… something… caught
caught her."

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.580
Caruso has kept a low profile since CSI: Miami
ended in 2012.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.140
Steven Bochco later opened up about his tumultuous
working relationship with Caruso, calling

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:30.689
the star's behavior on the NYPD Blue set "cancerous"
and alleging he had outrageous demands, like

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:34.580
$100,000 per episode and a 38-ft trailer.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.009
Dennis Franz

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:41.119
Though he's forever associated with cantankerous
recovering alcoholic Detective Andy Sipowicz,

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:46.020
Franz previously played the equally irritable
Lt. Norman Buntz on Hill Street Blues... and

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.479
its forgotten fish-out-of-water comedy spinoff
Beverly Hills Buntz.

00:01:49.479 --> 00:01:54.079
As Sipowicz, Franz scored four Emmys, and
one memorable nude shower scene.

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:58.549
Following NYPD Blue's final season, Franz
left showbiz to focus on a quiet life that

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:02.350
presumably doesn't involve smacking suspects
with phone books.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:07.229
He resurfaced at the 2016 Emmys, reuniting
with former costar Jimmy Smits to the delight

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:08.229
of fans.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.319
Maybe it's time for Netflix to greenlight
Sipowicz: The Frickin' Golden Years.

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:13.319
Jimmy Smits

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:18.599
L.A. Law star Jimmy Smits joined the cast
of NYPD Blue in season two as Sipowicz's partner

00:02:18.599 --> 00:02:22.200
Bobby Simone, after Caruso's John Kelly resigned
from the force.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.260
Simone's tragic death from a heart condition
made for one of the most moving episodes of

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.260
the series.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.180
Smits, on the other hand, is alive and well,
and recently appeared as Senator Donovan on

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.470
24: Legacy.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:37.150
Smits also had memorable runs on shows like
The West Wing, Sons of Anarchy and Dexter.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:41.420
He also returned to the character he played
in the Star Wars prequels, Senator Bail Organa,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.629
for 2016's hit film Rogue One.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.780
But the best role he's ever played?

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.480
Johnny Wilson, Conky Repairman, on Pee-Wee's
playhouse:

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.519
"Johnny Wilson, authorized Conky repairman
at your service, Miss?"

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:53.519
"Yvonne."

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:54.519
"Where's my..."

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.500
"Is that a wrench in your pocket?"

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.500
"Ah!

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.100
That's a wrench!

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.100
Thank you very much."

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.870
Kim Delaney

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.700
Actress Kim Delaney brought grit to the role
of Detective Diane Russell, whose battles

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.950
with alcoholism and tumultuous relationships
with fellow cops made for some juicy storylines.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.799
The part earned Delaney an Emmy for Best Supporting
Actress.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:16.489
After leaving Blue, Delaney took the lead
role on Steven Bochco's short-lived legal

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:21.020
drama Philly and had a brief run opposite
David Caruso on CSI: Miami.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:25.790
Following six seasons on the Lifetime series
Army Wives, Delaney again reunited with Bochco

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.719
for a role on his TNT series Murder in the
First.

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:31.409
Mark-Paul Gosselaar

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:36.030
Fans were surprised when Zack Morris himself,
Mark-Paul Gosselaar, joined NYPD Blue in season

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.250
9 as a replacement for departed cast member
Rick Schroder.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.720
Gosselaar's Detective John Clark held his
own opposite the cast and remained with the

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.380
show until it came to an end in 2005.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.769
Who knew Gosselaar would prove to be the best
actor among the Bayside bunch?

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:52.780
With roles on everything from Franklin and
Bash to the FOX baseball series Pitch, Gosselaar

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.180
has remained a reliable presence on the small
screen.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.160
He also relived his giant cellphone-toting
days in a Saved by the Bell reunion on The

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.340
Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.810
Gordon Clapp

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:06.810
With his constant motormouth and awkward demeanor,
Detective Greg Medavoy brought comic relief

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.209
to the 15th precinct.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:12.640
A regular on NYPD Blue throughout its entire
run, Medavoy grew to be a fan favorite and

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.700
an Emmy winner.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.850
Gordon Clapp continues to work in theater,
earning a Tony nomination for Glengarry Glen

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.260
Ross on Broadway, and on shows like Damages
and Elementary.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.440
These days he has a recurring role as Chaplain
Orlovsky on Chicago Fire.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.260
Nicholas Turturro

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.640
John Turturro's younger brother made a name
for himself on NYPD Blue, scoring an Emmy

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.030
nomination for his role as Detective James
Martinez.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:38.390
Martinez was a crucial part of the squad before
being promoted to sergeant in season 7 and

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.360
saying goodbye to the 15th precinct.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.910
Turturro returned to the "blue" brotherhood
for his role as Sgt.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:47.690
Renzulli on CBS' Blue Bloods, and his voice
can be heard as the ghostly superhero Deadman

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.630
in the Justice League Dark animated movie.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.010
"Batman's head of me?

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.010
Sweet!

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.300
Tell him I'm a fan of his too."

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.710
He also showed off his comedic chops in films
like Paul Blart: Mall Cop 2 and Bucky Larson:

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.230
Born to Be a Star.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.750
James McDaniel

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:06.140
As Lieutenant Arthur Fancy, James McDaniel
held the 15th Precinct together with his calm

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.610
yet commanding presence, eventually being
promoted to captain.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:13.530
McDaniel left the show after season eight,
and while the precinct had other captains,

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.390
they don't hold a candle to McDaniel.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:19.360
With a deep resume that includes theatrical
productions and films like Malcolm X and TV

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.420
shows like Sleepy Hollow and The Good Wife,
McDaniel has kept busy since hanging up his

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.420
gun and shield.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.630
He also has the dubious distinction of having
starred on Steven Bochco's infamous musical

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.780
police procedural Cop Rock.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.090
And rock it did not.

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.780
Henry Simmons

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:39.160
Joining Blue in its seventh season as Medavoy's
new partner Baldwin Jones, Henry Simmons was

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.490
one half of a formidable team, with Jones'
intensity and Medavoy's persistence working

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.870
in tandem to get confessions out of "skels."

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.000
Simmons is currently part of the Marvel TV
universe as Mack on Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.530
You may have also caught him on shows like
Ravenswood, and Man Up.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.190
Bill Brochtrup

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.190
As P.A.A.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:06:00.770
"Upstairs" John Irvin, Bill Brochtrup brought
heart, diversity, and subtle humor to what

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:02.860
could have been a thankless, forgettable role.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:07.340
Prior to Blue, Brochtrup was a regular on
Steven Bochco shows like Total Security and

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.520
the doomed cop comedy Public Morals.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.740
These days Brochtrup keeps busy in the theater
world and brings the same sensitivity he brought

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:18.520
to John to his role as psychologist Dr. Bowman
on TNT's Major Crimes.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.520
Sharon Lawrence

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.210
ADA Sylvia Costas was on the receiving end
of one of Sipowicz's most memorably profane

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:28.580
rants in the pilot episode of NYPD Blue, but
she eventually fell for his gruff charms and

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.960
married the ol' lug.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.860
Her murder during season six left Sipowicz
to raise their infant son alone.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:37.780
Actress Sharon Lawrence, who scored three
Emmy Nominations for her role, left the series

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.560
in 1996 to costar with Leah Remini on the
short-lived NBC sitcom Fired Up.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.310
A TV vet, she's had memorable roles on shows
like Desperate Housewives, Grey's Anatomy,

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:48.490
and Shameless.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.000
Charlotte Ross

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.160
Prior to NYPD Blue, Charlotte Ross cut her
teeth in the soap opera world and starred

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.000
on the short-lived FOX musical drama The Heights.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.250
She joined the cop drama in 2001, and made
a splash when her character Detective Connie

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:05.400
McDowell appeared partially nude in a controversial
2004 episode.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.781
The sweet-natured McDowell would eventually
melt grumpy ol' Sipowicz's heart, and the

00:07:08.781 --> 00:07:11.560
pair married and raised kids in the show's
later seasons.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.430
Ross has kept busy on television since Blue
ended, with turns on shows like Glee and Nashville.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:21.460
Arrow fans will recognize her as Felicity
Smoak's brassy mom Donna on the hit CW superhero

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:22.460
show.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.460
Thanks for watching!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.330
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.110
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

